  "Number": 7,
  "Question": "Which of the following equations does not have a solution?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\((x + 7)^2 = 0\\)",
    "B": "\\(|-3x| + 5 = 0\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\sqrt{-x} - 2 = 0\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\sqrt{x} - 8 = 0\\)",
    "E": "\\(|-3x| - 4 = 0\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "An absolute value is nonnegative. Therefore, for every real \\(x\\),\n\\[\n|-3x|+5\\ge 5>0.\n\\]\nThus the equation in B cannot have a solution.\n\nTo verify that it is the only such choice, one working value for each remaining equation is enough:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{A: }&x=-7, &&(-7+7)^2=0;\\\\\n\\text{C: }&x=-4, &&\\sqrt{-(-4)}-2=0;\\\\\n\\text{D: }&x=64, &&\\sqrt{64}-8=0;\\\\\n\\text{E: }&x=\\frac43, &&\\left|-3\\left(\\frac43\\right)\\right|-4=0.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe square roots used here have nonnegative radicands. Hence the equation without a solution is \\(|-3x|+5=0\\), choice B.",
